<article class="env-corollary" id="E03B1C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/E03B1C">Corollary <span data-tag="E03B1C">6.5.1.14</span>.</a> Let $f: X \rightarrow X'$ be a morphism in an $\infty $-topos $\calX $. Then $f$ is $(n+1)$-connective if and only if composition with $f$ induces a homotopy equivalence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[ \bHom _{\calX _{/X'}}(\id _{X'},Y) \rightarrow \bHom _{\calX _{/X'}}(f,Y) \]
</div>
  <p> for every $n$-truncated object $Y \in \calX _{/X'}$. </p>
</article>